# Email Template Redesign

The user wants the notification email to match the website's "liquid glass" and "neumorphic" aesthetic.
Current state: Basic HTML string in [sendDiagnosticEmail](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/app/actions/send-email.ts#7-72).

## Proposed Changes
### [Actions]
#### [MODIFY] [send-email.ts](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/app/actions/send-email.ts)
- Replace the simple HTML string with a robust, table-based HTML template.
- **Design Specs**:
    - **Background**: `#FAF9F6` (Main site background).
    - **Container**: Rounded corners, "Glass" effect simulation using borders (`border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.8)`) and soft shadows.
    - **Typography**: Sans-serif, dark gray text, Orange (`#f97316`) headers.
    - **Neumorphism**: Since email clients have limited CSS support for complex shadows (`box-shadow`), we will use comprehensive fallbacks (solid borders, simple background colors) that approximation the look.
    - **Structure**:
        - Header with Title/Logo placeholder.
        - Data sections organized in clean blocks.
        - Footer with subtle styling.

## Compatibility Note
- `backdrop-filter` is not supported in most email clients (Gmail, Outlook).
- `box-shadow` support is mixed.
- We will rely on **color palette** and **spacing** to evoke the feel, rather than depending on advanced CSS rendering.

## Verification Plan
- Since we cannot send actual emails in this environment, checking the code compilation and visually verifying the HTML structure (by potentially rendering it in a test page temporarily if needed, or just careful code review) will be the method.
